# Reanimated & gestures (Hermes / UI-thread)

When writing `react-native-reanimated` or `react-native-gesture-handler` code (worklets, `runOnJS`, `Gesture.*`, `useAnimatedStyle`):

## Required

1. Pass **stable** functions to `runOnJS` — `useCallback` (often with a ref for the latest parent callback).
2. Build `Gesture.*` trees inside **`useMemo`** (or an equivalent stable factory). Do not recreate pinch/pan/tap every render.
3. Do not pass fresh function literals from render into worklets / `runOnJS`.
4. Guard `runOnJS` handlers against unmount before `setState` or parent callbacks (mounted ref).

Reference patterns in this repo: `components/review/InteractiveStarRating.tsx`, `components/wine/LabelCropCanvas.tsx`.

## Optional hygiene

5. Use `?.` / `??` where values are truly optional — not as a substitute for (1)–(4), and not to hide real bugs.
